<main>
<section class="hero" id="home">
  <div>
    <div class="eyebrow"><span>●</span> AWS-powered online shopping chatbot</div>
    <h1>Shopping made<br><span>smarter.</span></h1>
    <p class="lead">ShopMate AI is a conversational online shopping assistant designed with Amazon Lex V2 to collect customer details, understand product requirements, manage quantity and confirm the request.</p>
    <div class="actions"><button class="primary" onclick="openChat()">Start Shopping →</button><a class="secondary" href="#about">Explore Project</a></div>
  </div>
  <div class="hero-card">
    <div class="chat-head"><div class="avatar">🤖</div><div><strong>ShopMate AI</strong><small>● Online assistant</small></div></div>
    <div class="chat">
      <div class="msg bot">Welcome to online shopping. May I have your name?</div>
      <div class="msg user">Atharva</div>
      <div class="msg bot">Please provide your email ID.</div>
      <div class="msg user">atharva@example.com</div>
      <div class="msg bot">Which product do you want and what quantity?</div>
    </div>
    <button class="chat-open" onclick="openChat()">Open AI Assistant</button>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="band">
  <div><strong>Amazon Lex V2</strong><small>Conversation engine</small></div>
  <div><strong>AWS Lambda</strong><small>Fulfillment & validation</small></div>
  <div><strong>Amazon CloudWatch</strong><small>Monitoring & logs</small></div>
  <div><strong>AWS CLI / Web UI</strong><small>Testing & management</small></div>
</div>

<section id="about">
  <div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">01 — Project Overview</div><h2>Online Shopping <span>Chatbot.</span></h2><p>The project implements a conversational shopping experience where the chatbot interacts with a customer, gathers required information and reaches a confirmation/fulfillment response.</p></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><span class="number">01</span><div class="icon">👤</div><h3>Customer Details</h3><p>Collect customer name, email ID, phone number and address as part of the conversation.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">02</span><div class="icon">📦</div><h3>Product Preferences</h3><p>Ask the customer for the product they want and the quantity required.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><span class="number">03</span><div class="icon">✓</div><h3>Confirmation</h3><p>Confirm the collected request and provide a final fulfillment response.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="features">
  <div class="heading center"><div class="eyebrow">02 — Core Features</div><h2>Everything in one <span>conversation.</span></h2><p>The website presents the complete chatbot functionality in a clear, professional interface.</p></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">💬</div><h3>Conversational Interaction</h3><p>Customers communicate naturally with the shopping assistant instead of navigating a complex form.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">🧾</div><h3>Slot-Based Collection</h3><p>The Lex conversation can collect the required values through configured slots such as name, email, phone, address, product and quantity.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">⚡</div><h3>Fulfillment</h3><p>After the required information and confirmation are received, the bot reaches its fulfillment response.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="how">
  <div class="flow">
    <div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">03 — How It Works</div><h2>From hello to <span>confirmation.</span></h2><p>The documented conversation flow is represented below as a simple customer journey.</p></div>
    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step"><span class="stepnum">01</span><div><h3>Customer starts the conversation</h3><p>The user begins an online shopping interaction.</p></div><span class="arrow">›</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="stepnum">02</span><div><h3>Name, email, phone & address</h3><p>The bot collects customer information through slots.</p></div><span class="arrow">›</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="stepnum">03</span><div><h3>Product & quantity</h3><p>The customer provides the desired product and quantity.</p></div><span class="arrow">›</span></div>
      <div class="step"><span class="stepnum">04</span><div><h3>Confirmation & fulfillment</h3><p>The request is confirmed and the final response is returned.</p></div><span class="arrow">✓</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="aws">
  <div class="heading center"><div class="eyebrow">04 — AWS Architecture</div><h2>Built with <span>AWS.</span></h2><p>The project report identifies Amazon Lex V2, AWS Lambda and Amazon CloudWatch as core services. DynamoDB and S3 are listed as optional storage services.</p></div>
  <div class="arch">
    <div class="node"><div class="icon">🛍</div><strong>ShopMate UI</strong><small>Web Interface</small></div><span class="arr">→</span>
    <div class="node"><div class="icon">🤖</div><strong>Amazon Lex V2</strong><small>Conversation & intents</small></div><span class="arr">→</span>
    <div class="node"><div class="icon">λ</div><strong>AWS Lambda</strong><small>Fulfillment</small></div><span class="arr">→</span>
    <div class="node"><div class="icon">☁</div><strong>CloudWatch</strong><small>Monitoring & logs</small></div>
  </div>
  <div class="arch" style="margin-top:15px">
    <div class="node"><div class="icon">🗄</div><strong>DynamoDB</strong><small>Optional storage</small></div>
    <div class="node"><div class="icon">▣</div><strong>Amazon S3</strong><small>Optional storage</small></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="lex">
  <div class="heading"><div class="eyebrow">05 — Amazon Lex V2</div><h2>Conversation <span>intelligence.</span></h2><p>Amazon Lex V2 is the chatbot service used for the project's conversational flow. The project configures a bot, language, intent, sample utterances and slots before building and testing it.</p></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">🎯</div><h3>Intent</h3><p>The shopping intent represents the customer's online shopping request and controls the conversation flow.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">🔤</div><h3>Sample Utterances</h3><p>Example customer phrases are configured so Lex can recognize how users may start the shopping interaction.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">🧩</div><h3>Slots</h3><p>Slots are used to collect required customer and order values during the conversation.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="steps">
  <div class="darkbox">
    <div class="eyebrow">06 — Implementation Guide</div>
    <h2>Project setup <span>steps.</span></h2>
    <p class="lead">The following nine stages follow the structure documented in the project report.</p>
    <div class="timeline">
      <article><b>STEP 01</b><h3>Sign in to AWS Lex V2</h3><p>Open Amazon Lex V2 through the AWS Management Console.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 02</b><h3>Configure Bot Settings</h3><p>Configure the initial bot settings and basic information.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 03</b><h3>Add Language</h3><p>Add and configure the language used by the bot.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 04</b><h3>Add Intent Details</h3><p>Configure the shopping intent and its conversation behavior.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 05</b><h3>Add Sample Utterances</h3><p>Add example phrases customers may use to start the intent.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 06</b><h3>Build Bot</h3><p>Build the Lex bot after configuring its conversation resources.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 07</b><h3>Test Draft</h3><p>Use the Lex test interface to check the draft conversation.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 08</b><h3>Add Slots</h3><p>Configure customer and product information slots required by the flow.</p></article>
      <article><b>STEP 09</b><h3>Build, Update & Test</h3><p>Build the final bot, update resources and test the completed conversation.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="heading center"><div class="eyebrow">07 — Technology Stack</div><h2>Project <span>technologies.</span></h2></div>
  <div class="grid">
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">🌐</div><h3>HTML / CSS / JavaScript</h3><p>Professional responsive web interface for presenting and interacting with the chatbot.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">☁</div><h3>AWS Services</h3><p>Amazon Lex V2, AWS Lambda and Amazon CloudWatch form the documented AWS foundation.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><div class="icon">🛠</div><h3>Testing Tools</h3><p>AWS CLI and Lex Web UI are included in the documented project testing approach.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="heading center"><div class="eyebrow">08 — Project Outcome</div><h2>A complete conversational <span>shopping flow.</span></h2><p>The finished project demonstrates how a customer can move from an initial greeting through information collection, product selection, quantity and confirmation.</p></div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="darkbox" style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:30px">
    <div><div class="eyebrow">09 — Try It</div><h2>Experience ShopMate <span>AI.</span></h2><p class="lead">Open the assistant and explore the shopping conversation.</p></div>
